values ('c3d4e5f6-7a8b-4d23-8e23-3f4a5b6c7d33', 'introduction-to-anthropology', 'Introduction to Anthropology', 'This course introduces anthropology as the holistic and comparative study of humanity. Students explore cultural anthropology, biological anthropology, archaeology, linguistic anthropology, ethnographic methods, ethics, human evolution, material culture, language, kinship, religion, gender, race, colonialism, globalization, health, environment, digital life, and applied anthropology. The course emphasizes cultural relativism, evidence, fieldwork, ethical responsibility, and the public value of anthropological thinking.');

